+# Live compatibility research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- “VCF PowerCLI” — Broadcom Developer Portal — https://developer.broadcom.com/powercli — informed the module prerequisite and the choice to use the VCF PowerCLI SDK surface.
+- “Product Interoperability Matrix” — Broadcom — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — informed the vCenter, ESXi, NSX, and Live Site Recovery compatibility gates and the need to preserve explicit intermediate hops.
+- “Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1” — Broadcom Knowledge Base — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — informed the VCF 9.1 component sequencing and management-services placement.
+- “Build numbers and versions of VMware NSX/NSX-T Data Center” — Broadcom Knowledge Base — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/317797/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-nsx.html — informed the NSX 4.x-to-9.1 version checkpoints.
+- “VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1: Transition from standalone SRM and VR 9.0.2” — Broadcom Knowledge Base — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/vcf-protection-and-recovery-91-transitio.html — informed the transition from Live Site Recovery to the unified 9.1 protection appliance.
+- “VMware Cloud Foundation Installer API Reference Guide / SddcSpec” — Broadcom Developer Portal — https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/vcf-installer-api/latest/data-structures/SddcSpec/ — informed the greenfield management-domain document shape and its VCF Operations and Automation fields.
+- “VMware Cloud Foundation API Specifications” — Broadcom Developer Portal — https://developer.broadcom.com/sdks/vcf-api-specification/latest/ — confirmed the published 9.1 API-specification release used to pin installer validation.
+- “VMware Live Site Recovery” — Broadcom Developer Portal — https://developer.broadcom.com/sdks/site-recovery-manager-srm/latest/ — informed the Live Site Recovery upgrade/pairing migration gate.
+
+The live pages were used to check current product and API context. Exact grading targets, intermediate versions, order, gates, and sizes follow the supplied pinned compatibility snapshot so later matrix edits cannot change the artifact.
